# APK Analyzer

Comprehensive APK file analysis: metadata extraction, permission auditing, signature verification, component inspection, library detection, and security assessment.

## Step 1 — Basic Metadata

```bash
APK="path/to/your.apk"
aapt dump badging "$APK" | grep -E "^package:|^sdkVersion:|^targetSdkVersion:|^application-label:"
```

Extract: package name, version code/name, min SDK, target SDK, app label.

## Step 2 — Permission Audit

```bash
aapt dump permissions "$APK"
```

Classify every permission into one of three tiers:

| Tier | Examples |
|------|---------|
| **Dangerous** | CAMERA, READ_CONTACTS, ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION, RECORD_AUDIO, READ_SMS, READ_PHONE_STATE |
| **High-Risk** | RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED, SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW, BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE, INSTALL_PACKAGES |
| **Normal** | INTERNET, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, ACCESS_WIFI_STATE |

Output format:
```
[DANGEROUS] (N)  ✗ READ_CONTACTS  ✗ CAMERA  ...
[HIGH-RISK] (N)  ⚠ RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED  ...
[NORMAL]    (N)  ✓ INTERNET  ...
```

## Step 3 — Signature Verification

```bash
apksigner verify --verbose --print-certs "$APK" 2>&1 | \
  grep -E "Verified|Signer|Subject|Issuer|SHA-256|Expir"
```

Check:
- Schemes used: V1 (JAR) / V2 (APK) / V3
- Certificate subject, issuer, expiry date
- SHA-256 fingerprint — compare against known debug keystore:
  `61:ED:37:7E:85:D3:86:A8:DF:EE:6B:86:4B:D8:5B:27:44:9D:42:1D` (SHA-1 of debug cert)

## Step 4 — Manifest Component Analysis

```bash
apktool d "$APK" -o apk_out --no-src -f 2>/dev/null
```

For each component type (activity / service / receiver / provider), identify:
- `exported="true"` without a `android:permission` — unprotected entry point
- Sensitive implicit intent filters (BOOT_COMPLETED, NEW_OUTGOING_CALL, etc.)

Security flags to check:
```bash
grep -E "debuggable|allowBackup|cleartext|usesCleartextTraffic" apk_out/AndroidManifest.xml
```

## Step 5 — DEX & MultiDex

```bash
unzip -l "$APK" | grep "\.dex"           # count DEX files
dexdump -f "$APK" | grep -E "class_defs_size|method_ids_size"
```

Note class count and whether multidex is used (> 1 DEX file).

## Step 6 — Native Libraries & SDK Detection

```bash
unzip -l "$APK" | grep "\.so$"           # list native libs
```

Report supported ABIs (`armeabi-v7a`, `arm64-v8a`, `x86`, `x86_64`).

Detect common frameworks from lib names:

| Pattern | Framework |
|---------|-----------|
| `libflutter.so` | Flutter |
| `libreactnativejni.so` | React Native |
| `libweexjss.so` | Weex |
| `libxamarin*.so` | Xamarin |

Detect SDKs from DEX class prefixes (via jadx or dexdump):
`com.google.firebase`, `com.facebook.`, `io.branch.`, `com.appsflyer.`, `com.adjust.sdk`, `io.sentry.`

## Step 7 — Security Audit

Check each item; flag with severity:

| Check | Risk |
|-------|------|
| `debuggable="true"` | CRITICAL — must not ship in release |
| Signed with debug keystore | HIGH — not for production |
| Exported component without `android:permission` | HIGH |
| `allowBackup="true"` | MEDIUM — sensitive data may be extracted |
| Cleartext traffic permitted | MEDIUM |
| No V2/V3 signature | MEDIUM |
| No SSL pinning detected | INFO |

```bash
# Hardcoded secrets scan
unzip -p "$APK" "res/values/strings.xml" | \
  grep -iE "(api_key|secret|token|password|apikey)" | head -20
```

